  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana has ratified 51 Conventions, of which 37 are in force and is in the process of ratifying more conventions. In addition, ratifying ILO conventions places reporting obligations on the application of ILS to the ILO by the member states. Even though, in recent years, Ghana has met its reporting obligations, however there are pending reports for 2024 and 2025. Further, the National Labour Laws are obsolete and need to revise to address the evolving issues in the world of work in line with ILS.
The intervention supports the strengthening of the government and the social partners through technical advice, training with the objective of getting them to ratify more conventions, meet its reporting obligations and revise it national labour laws</narrative>
  </description>
